---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Topbar from '../components/Topbar.astro';
import FileTransferArticles from '../components/FileTransferArticles.astro';

const pageDescription =
	'Privacy notes for Onlne File Share: how access keys, temporary file links, uploads, and shared file metadata work.';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy - Temporary File Sharing | Onlne File Share"
	description={pageDescription}
	keywords="file sharing privacy, secure file transfer, temporary access key, private file sharing"
>
	<main class="page-shell">
		<Topbar active="privacy" />

		<section class="privacy-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
			<h1>Privacy policy for temporary file sharing.</h1>
			<p>Onlne File Share is designed for temporary file handoff. Upload a file, receive an access key, and share that key only with people who should be able to download it.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="privacy-grid" aria-label="Privacy details">
			<article><span>01</span><h2>Uploaded files</h2><p>Files are stored so they can be downloaded by someone with the access key or file link.</p></article>
			<article><span>02</span><h2>Access keys</h2><p>Treat access keys like temporary passwords. Anyone with a valid key may retrieve the file.</p></article>
			<article><span>03</span><h2>Temporary links</h2><p>Download links include an expiration time. After expiry, the same link should no longer be used.</p></article>
			<article><span>04</span><h2>Metadata</h2><p>The app displays basic file details such as name, size, content type, creation time, and expiry.</p></article>
			<article><span>05</span><h2>What to avoid</h2><p>Do not upload sensitive documents unless you are comfortable sharing the generated key privately.</p></article>
			<article><span>06</span><h2>Your responsibility</h2><p>Only share keys through trusted channels, and avoid posting them in public places.</p></article>
		</section>

		<section class="privacy-copy" aria-labelledby="privacy-seo-title">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sharing safely</p>
			<h2 id="privacy-seo-title">A key is like a short-lived password</h2>
			<p>
				A generated key or link should be treated like a temporary password. If someone has it,
				they may be able to open the file until it expires.
			</p>
			<p>
				Share keys in private chats or email, not public comments or posts. For sensitive files,
				pause first and decide whether a temporary browser upload is the right choice.
			</p>
			<p>
				Privacy for online file sharing is mostly about who can reach the key. When you upload a
				file, the page gives you a way to pass access to someone else. That key or link is useful
				because it is simple, but it should not be treated like a public label. Send it only to the
				person who should have the file, and avoid putting it in places where it can be copied by
				people you do not know.
			</p>
			<p>
				Onlne File Share is built for temporary handoffs, not permanent storage. Keep your own copy
				of anything important. If you are sending a school project, a work document, a photo set, a
				video, or a ZIP archive, make sure the recipient has what they need before you forget about
				the upload. Temporary links are helpful, but they are not a replacement for backing up your
				own files.
			</p>
			<p>
				People may find this site while searching for secure file transfer, online file transfer,
				online file sharing, online file drop, or even misspelled searches like onlne file shaing
				and online file frop. No matter what phrase brought you here, the privacy habit is the
				same: the file is only as private as the way you share the key. If the key is forwarded,
				screenshot, pasted into a public group, or posted online, other people may be able to use
				it too.
			</p>
			<p>
				The page may show basic file details such as the file name, size, type, upload time, and
				expiry time. These details help the sender and recipient confirm that they are handling the
				right file. Before you download something, check the name and size. Before you share
				something, check that you selected the correct file. Small checks like this prevent a lot
				of mistakes.
			</p>
			<p>
				Some files should not be shared casually. Legal documents, IDs, private financial records,
				password lists, medical files, and confidential work material deserve extra care. If you
				are unsure, use a more controlled method or talk to the recipient first. For everyday file
				drops, quick transfers, and files that are safe to send through a temporary link, this site
				keeps the process straightforward.
			</p>
			<p>
				The simplest rule is this: upload only what you mean to share, check the result, and send
				the access key through a channel you trust. That is the foundation of safer online file
				sharing, whether you call it a fileshare, a file transfer link, or a browser file drop.
			</p>
		</section>

		<FileTransferArticles />
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.privacy-hero, .privacy-grid, .privacy-copy { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
	.privacy-hero, .privacy-grid, .privacy-copy { width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 64px)); margin: 0 auto; }
	.privacy-hero { padding: 72px 0 32px; }
	.privacy-grid span { margin: 0; color: var(--accent); font-family: "Geist Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, monospace; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; }
	h1, h2, p { margin-top: 0; }
	h1 { max-width: 760px; margin: 14px 0 18px; font-size: clamp(46px, 7vw, 84px); line-height: 0.96; color: var(--ink); }
	.privacy-hero p:last-child { max-width: 680px; color: var(--body); font-size: 18px; line-height: 29px; }
	.privacy-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-bottom: 40px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--card-bg); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
	.privacy-grid article { min-height: 230px; padding: 22px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.privacy-grid article:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 0; }
	.privacy-grid article:nth-last-child(-n + 3) { border-bottom: 0; }
	.privacy-grid h2 { margin: 64px 0 10px; font-size: 22px; color: var(--ink); }
	.privacy-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 23px; }
	.privacy-copy { margin-bottom: 48px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--card-bg); box-shadow: var(--shadow); padding: 28px; }
	.privacy-copy h2 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px); line-height: 1.1; color: var(--ink); }
	.privacy-copy p { color: var(--body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 27px; }
	.privacy-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
	@media (max-width: 860px) { .privacy-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .privacy-grid article:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 1px solid var(--line); } .privacy-grid article:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; } .privacy-grid article:nth-last-child(-n + 3) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } .privacy-grid article:nth-last-child(-n + 2) { border-bottom: 0; } }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .privacy-hero, .privacy-grid, .privacy-copy { width: calc(100% - 32px); } .privacy-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .privacy-grid article, .privacy-grid article:nth-child(2n), .privacy-grid article:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } .privacy-grid article:last-child { border-bottom: 0; } }
</style>
